My weekly review notes are named like 2026-W40 and start with this DataviewJS. Make me a template at Templates/Weekly review.md that does the same with Dashy, so I can stop using Dataview:

```dataviewjs
const name = dv.current().file.name;              // e.g. 2026-W40
const start = moment(name, "GGGG-[W]WW").startOf("isoWeek");
const end = start.clone().endOf("isoWeek");
const days = dv.pages('"Diary"').where(p => p.file.day && p.file.day >= start && p.file.day <= end);
const avg = f => { const v = days.map(p => p[f]).filter(x => typeof x === "number"); return v.length ? Math.round(v.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / v.length) : "-"; };
dv.paragraph(`Sleep ${avg("sleep_score")} · Steps ${avg("steps")} · Gym ${days.where(p => p.gym).length} days`);
```

Replace this DataviewJS heatmap with Dashy, in a new note called Training year:

```dataviewjs
// Colour each day by the sport with the most minutes; darker = more minutes that day in total.
const mins = v => typeof v === "number" ? v : v ? dv.duration(String(v)).as("minutes") : 0;
dv.view("scripts/heatmap", { pages: dv.pages('"Diary"'), sports: {
  run: p => mins(p.run_time), bike: p => mins(p.bike_time), swim: p => mins(p.swim_time) } });
```

